## Program Outcome

Eligible Tool Shed App Server work cannot be silently executed outside its selected backend. Every
selection uses one correlated dispatch lifecycle and reaches completed, controlled pre-mutation
fallback, or reconciliation-required state. Unresolved eligible dispatch debt is visible and blocks
applicable campaign, PRM, and Work5 closure. The behavior is qualified on fresh and upgraded
supported targets, released, production-verified, and recursively reconciled.

## M1-ATOMIC-CORRELATED-DISPATCH — Make selection inseparable from accountable execution

Status: ready
Required Endpoint: Work2
Depends on: none

Outcome: Replace advisory select-then-trust behavior with one normal dispatch entry point or a
bounded dispatch lease. Carry one content-free correlation ID through opportunity, attempt, and a
terminal completion, fallback, or reconciliation-required event. Preserve strict and default-mode
failure semantics without replay after possible mutation.

Gate: `G1-ATOMIC-CORRELATED-DISPATCH`

Candidate campaign: `build-atomic-correlated-app-server-dispatch`.

## M2-CLOSEOUT-ENFORCEMENT-AND-RELEASE — Prevent bypass and prove the full contract

Status: waiting
Required Endpoint: Work5
Depends on: M1-ATOMIC-CORRELATED-DISPATCH

Outcome: Detect orphaned or expired selections in bounded reporting and Doctor, prevent applicable
campaign, PRM, release-cohort, and Work5 completion while dispatch debt remains, prove controlled
fallback and post-mutation reconciliation, qualify fresh and upgraded installations on supported
Linux and Windows targets, and release only after one real eligible operation produces a complete
correlated chain.

Gate: `G2-CLOSEOUT-ENFORCEMENT-QUALIFIED-AND-RELEASED`

Candidate campaign: `enforce-and-qualify-app-server-dispatch-closure`.

## Acceptance Gates

### G1-ATOMIC-CORRELATED-DISPATCH

- The supported eligible routes cannot record `selected` and then proceed through an unaccounted
  GUI implementation path.
- Opportunity, attempt, completion, fallback, and reconciliation handoff use one correlation ID.
- Every selection reaches exactly one controlled terminal state or remains explicit pending debt.
- Default-mode pre-mutation failure records a controlled category and continues the same GUI action.
- Explicit `--app-server` failure remains fail-closed.
- Possible post-mutation failure never replays work and requires workspace reconciliation.

### G2-CLOSEOUT-ENFORCEMENT-QUALIFIED-AND-RELEASED

- Bounded reporting and strict Doctor detect orphaned, expired, duplicated, malformed, and
  contradictory dispatch lifecycles without retaining content.
- Applicable campaign, PRM, release-cohort, and Work5 closeout refuse unresolved dispatch debt.
- GUI-native and unsupported roles remain exempt through controlled reason codes.
- Tests cover selected-to-completed, selected-to-fallback, mutation-uncertain reconciliation,
  attempted bypass, crash/lease expiry, idempotent recovery, and legacy-event compatibility.
- Fresh and upgraded Linux and Windows qualification, full repository validation, checkpoint/rebuild,
  exact-SHA release gates, production verification, and one real eligible App Server operation pass.
- The campaign, roadmap, and project-map outcome chain is terminal, satisfied, reconciled, and
  recursively closed after release evidence exists.

## Recovery Contract

- Before mutation, a controlled App Server failure may fall back immediately in default mode and
  must close the same correlation as `fallback`.
- After possible mutation, record `reconciliation-required`, inspect the existing Git and mutation
  journal, reconcile once in GUI, and never replay the App Server step.
- On process loss, an expired lease becomes explicit dispatch debt; recovery either resumes the
  still-safe dispatch or records the appropriate terminal disposition without inventing execution.
- Legacy schema events remain bounded historical evidence and are not rewritten into false chains.

## Program Constraints

- Reuse the existing selector, dispatcher, orchestration, JSONL events, Doctor, Hybrid outcome
  reconciliation, release cohort, and closeout mechanisms.
- Add no server, database, daemon, hosted mutation route, or content-bearing telemetry.
- Keep discussion, brainstorming, qualification gates, unsupported roles, and other declared
  GUI-native work outside App Server execution.
- Do not infer unavailable GUI token usage or treat token reporting as the enforcement boundary.
- Keep the two campaigns independently verifiable and stop M1 at Work2 before publication.

## Verification Strategy

- Use focused selector, dispatcher, telemetry, crash-recovery, Doctor, closeout, and reconciliation
  tests for M1 and M2.
- Reproduce the observed orphan-selection bypass and prove closeout rejects it.
- Reproduce the observed over-budget planning context as a controlled pre-mutation fallback.
- Qualify clean install and historical upgrade behavior on the disposable Linux and Windows test
  beds before the exact candidate is released.
- Require exact-SHA CI, release provenance, production observation, and recursive outcome audit.

## Next Route

Execute `build-atomic-correlated-app-server-dispatch` as the bounded M1 Work2 campaign. Do not add
closeout enforcement, cross-platform release qualification, publication, or production delivery to M1.
